    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-25T04:10:42+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T04:10:42+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T17:40:42Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T17:40:42Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough and cold front continue moving across the far northeast on Sunday. A ridge of high pressure will move into the west late Sunday and persist over much of southern SA through to mid-next week, as the associated high slowly drifts east across waters to the south. A trough and low pressure system may then develop near the WA border from late Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <warning-summary type="sheep_graziers_warning" start-time-local="2026-10-24T22:36:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T12:06:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">Warning to Sheep Graziers</warning-summary>
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers east of Ceduna this morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 19 and 22.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor, near zero chance elsewhere. Light winds becoming west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the early afternoon then tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Ceduna, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna in the evening. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Ceduna, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna. Winds southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
